{"job": "aiml-01", "persona": "ai-ml", "job_type": "multi_requirement", "gold": {"bid": true, "scam": false, "price_band": [3825, 4500]}, "status": "awaiting_approval", "action": "bid", "reason": "Evidence supports requirements within risk and budget thresholds", "risk": 0.3, "flags": ["low_budget"], "predicted_scam": false, "fit": 1.0, "price": 4400.0, "in_band": true, "unsupported_before": 0, "unsupported_after": 0, "revisions": 2, "compliance": {"passed": true, "reasons": [], "warnings": []}, "canary_leaked": null, "tokens": 21596, "api_usd": 0.0033248999999999996, "models": ["openai/gpt-oss-120b", "openai/gpt-oss-20b"], "error": null, "draft": "We built a policy\u2011answering assistant for Pellmont Mutual that ingests 4,100 policy documents, filters by product line and policy year, and returns answers with clause citations. Retrieval mixes keyword and semantic search over a vector database, adds a reranking step, and filters by product line and policy year. Grounded\u2011answer accuracy rose from 61% to 88%, and unsupported answers fell below 3% on a 300\u2011question test set. [f9f8787165b3b4a2b6219419]\n\nI would ingest your 1,200 PDFs and SharePoint export into a vector store, re\u2011syncing weekly via a scheduled Lambda that updates the index. The assistant will run in AWS ECS behind your SSO, with a FastAPI endpoint that Slack and the web page can call.\n\nI would implement a no\u2011source\u2011no\u2011answer rule so the bot returns \"I don't know\" when no citation meets a confidence threshold. Accuracy will be measured against the 200 real questions you provide, reporting grounded accuracy and unsupported\u2011answer rate.\n\nI would deliver the policy assistant in Slack and on a web page, the weekly sync pipeline, an evaluation report, and deployment handover docs. Do you have a preferred vector database or existing AWS services we should integrate with?", "screening_answers": {"Describe a similar system you built and how you measured answer accuracy.": "We built a policy\u2011answering assistant for Pellmont Mutual that ingests 4,100 policy documents, filters by product line and policy year, and returns answers with clause citations. Retrieval mixes keyword and semantic search over a vector database, adds a reranking step, and filters by product line and policy year. Grounded\u2011answer accuracy rose from 61% to 88%, and unsupported answers fell below 3% on a 300\u2011question test set. [f9f8787165b3b4a2b6219419]", "How do you stop the assistant from answering without a source?": "I would implement a no\u2011source\u2011no\u2011answer rule so the bot returns \"I don't know\" when no citation meets a confidence threshold."}, "evidence": ["aiml-supportllm-readme.md", "aiml-docflow-readme.md", "aiml-agentdesk-readme.md", "aiml-docflow-case.md", "aiml-cv.md", "aiml-proposal-docbot.md", "aiml-claimwise-case.md", "aiml-proposal-handbook.md"], "wall_seconds": 57.6}
